Fixed. The bug was in src/resources/storage.ts:22-28 — `clampToStorageCap` clamped wood and stone with `Math.min(value, cap)` but passed food through unchanged (`food: resources.food`), so food could stockpile past the storage limit forever. Since the clamp runs after every production turn (src/sim/turn.ts:19-20), that one line was the entire leak.

Change: food is now clamped identically to the other resources, `food: Math.min(resources.food, cap)`, and I removed the stale "BUG" comment plus a comment in `utilizationOf` that referenced the food-only over-cap case (which can no longer happen).

Verified: npm run test (15/15 pass) and npm run typecheck both clean.


